TASK 6 — Ansible playbooks and inventory (install Tomcat + deploy WAR)

Create ansible/inventories/hosts.ini:

[app]
<APP_NODE_PUBLIC_IP> ansible_user=ubuntu ansible_ssh_private_key_file=~/Downloads/surjan-key.pem

ansible/playbooks/install_tomcat.yml
- name: Install Java and Tomcat on app node
  hosts: app
  become: yes
  tasks:
    - name: Update APT
      apt:
        update_cache: yes

    - name: Install default-jdk and unzip
      apt:
        name:
          - default-jdk
          - unzip
        state: present

    - name: Create tomcat directory
      file:
        path: /opt/tomcat
        state: directory
        owner: root
        group: root
        mode: '0755'

    - name: Download Tomcat 9
      get_url:
        url: "https://downloads.apache.org/tomcat/tomcat-9/v9.0.65/bin/apache-tomcat-9.0.65.tar.gz"
        dest: /tmp/tomcat9.tar.gz
      # (You can update the version number; official downloads: tomcat.apache.org). 
      # See Tomcat downloads page for latest 9.x. :contentReference[oaicite:4]{index=4}

    - name: Extract Tomcat
      unarchive:
        src: /tmp/tomcat9.tar.gz
        dest: /opt/tomcat
        remote_src: yes
        creates: /opt/tomcat/apache-tomcat-9.0.65

    - name: Create symlink to tomcat
      file:
        src: /opt/tomcat/apache-tomcat-9.0.65
        dest: /opt/tomcat/latest
        state: link

    - name: Start Tomcat
      shell: "nohup /opt/tomcat/latest/bin/startup.sh >/dev/null 2>&1 &"
      args:
        creates: /opt/tomcat/latest/bin/startup.sh

ansible/playbooks/deploy_war.yml
- name: Deploy application WAR to Tomcat
  hosts: app
  become: yes
  tasks:
    - name: Ensure webapps directory exists
      file:
        path: /opt/tomcat/latest/webapps
        state: directory

    - name: Copy WAR from Jenkins workspace to app node (example path)
      copy:
        src: /var/lib/jenkins/workspace/surjan-addressbook-cicd-project/target/*.war
        dest: /opt/tomcat/latest/webapps/
        mode: '0644'

    - name: Restart Tomcat
      shell: "/opt/tomcat/latest/bin/shutdown.sh || true; sleep 3; /opt/tomcat/latest/bin/startup.sh"


How you will run Ansible from Jenkins: place the hosts.ini and playbooks on the Jenkins server (or keep them in repo and checkout during pipeline). From the Jenkins master you can run:

